A||||7||GILLICK||INSURANCE!||||1||
Z||000000||GILLICK||05-28-2001||10:09 PM||||Hello everyone.<P>I was contemplating doing some mods to my fiero, and something crossed my mind.<P>If a mod fiero was in an accident, either at fault or not, would the insurance company replace the modified parts, engine etc?<P>Just wondering, any stories or info.<P>Thanks <P>------------------<BR>John D. Gillick<BR>jgillick@swbell.net||||reg||1
Z||000001||skitime||05-28-2001||10:22 PM||||My guess is no unless you have the car insured for a predetermined amount.  I am having my car appraised so the they will insure it for the appraised value rather than the blue book value.<P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL><BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pictures-1_5.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||GILLICK||05-28-2001||10:37 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by skitime:<BR><B>My guess is no unless you have the car insured for a predetermined amount.  I am having my car appraised so the they will insure it for the appraised value rather than the blue book value.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Thanks,<P>Beautiful car.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||05-28-2001||11:05 PM||||Check with your insurance company, Some will replace items if you have a receipt for them or they will add to the value of the car. Not all of them do it. It is actually better to have it appraised.||||reg||1
Z||000004||SPDFREK||05-28-2001||11:13 PM||||when I had my Nova insured (came as a 350cid/w 350 tranny and is now a 383 stroker with a 5 speed manual tubbed. 450 hp-11.54 in the 1/4 @ 118mph) I had to have it insured for the appraised value. I no longer have Insurance on the car because I race on the strip which voids all Insurance policies I have seen so far.Hint, if you plan to drive every day, DONT race semi professional or otherwise. (no street driving anymore    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> )But, I have the Fiero now! corners much better! LOL<P>[This message has been edited by SPDFREK (edited 05-28-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by SPDFREK (edited 05-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Alex2004||05-28-2001||11:48 PM||||I was wondering the same thing, since i have an 84 SE that looks like an 86 GT.... Thanks for the info!<P>Alex...||||reg||2
Z||000006||fierofreek2001||05-29-2001||01:07 AM||||at GEICO ... if your car is totalled in a wreck, and you file a claim , you should get a check for whatever your car is appraised at... then u can go buy whatever you want to buy with that check||||reg||1
Z||000007||tgowens||05-29-2001||02:03 AM||||Check with the insurance companies in your area. Some will add a rider for modifications while others will work with an appraised value. Some states will allow you to insure the car as an "antique" (usually through a broker) (pending miles driven, etc.) which will cover any modifications (I have one of mine insured this way)<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero/index.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>                <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero/3GTS_SIG.gif">                 </A>||||reg||1
